```
// Same import base SFCC's own swatch-group/swatch.jsx uses for its `RouteLink`, and the same
// reasoning zimmColourSwatch/index.tsx already documents: a router `Link` delivers "URL updates
// without a full page reload" for real. There is no overrides/.../link equivalent to reuse
// instead — confirmed none exists (see .claude/rules/overrideStyling.md's own note on this).
```

**The problem:** the underlying fact is true — `overrides/app/components/link/` genuinely doesn't exist on disk, confirmed. But the citation is backwards: `.claude/rules/overrideStyling.md`'s "The SFCC bridge pattern" section (read it yourself, around its own lines 173-193) doesn't confirm the override is absent — it actually asserts the opposite, that `link/index.tsx` "already" exists using a specific named-export split pattern (an assertion that section itself is already known to be stale/incorrect elsewhere, per that same doc's own text a few lines later: *"An earlier revision of this paragraph cited theme/components/imageGallery.ts / swatchGroup.ts... neither file has ever existed"* — i.e. that section has a known history of asserting things about override state that turned out false). So citing it as the thing that "confirms" no link override exists gets the direction backwards.

**The fix:** remove the citation to `overrideStyling.md`. Keep the factual claim (no `overrides/.../link` equivalent exists) stated plainly, based on direct verification, not a citation to a doc section that doesn't actually establish it. Something like:

```
// Same import base SFCC's own swatch-group/swatch.jsx uses for its `RouteLink`, and the same
// reasoning zimmColourSwatch/index.tsx already documents: a router `Link` delivers "URL updates
// without a full page reload" for real. Confirmed directly (no overrides/app/components/link/
// directory exists on disk) — there is no overrides/.../link equivalent to reuse instead.
```

(Use your own judgement on exact wording if this doesn't fit the surrounding comment style, but the citation to `overrideStyling.md` must be removed, and no new citation invented in its place — state it as a direct, verified fact.)

**Do not touch** anything else in this file — no logic, no other comment, nothing structural.

When done, quote the exact before/after, confirm `npx tsc --noEmit` is clean, and confirm `npx vitest run overrides/app/components/ui-kits/molecules/zimmProductCardContent/index.test.tsx` still passes. Do not stage, do not commit.

